.TH tkutablelist n 0.5 tkutils
.SH "tkutils::tkutablelist (optional)"
.PP
A multi\-column table built on the \fBTablelist\fR megawidget (from tklib): a rows/columns API, click\-to\-sort headers, editable cells, selection helpers, per\-column configuration, optional frozen title columns, CSV loading via tclutils \fBtucsv\fR, and display of a tclutils \fBtunotes\fR store.
.PP
OPTIONAL widget \-\- not listed in the tkutils umbrella itself, but \fBtkutils::tkufilelist\fR (in the umbrella) requires it, so loading the umbrella loads it too and needs Tablelist. Standalone: require it directly once Tablelist is installed (e.g. \fBapt install tklib\fR):
.CS
package require tkutils::tkutablelist
.CE
.SS API
.CS
set w [::tkutils::tkutablelist::widget .w ?-columns {t...}? ?-stretch all? \
        ?-titlecolumns N? ?-sortable 1? ?-editable 0? ?-selectmode extended? \
        ?-exportselection 0? ?-stripes COLOR? ?-selectcommand cmd? \
        ?-doublecommand cmd?]
# -exportselection defaults to 0 (PRIMARY not cleared by menus); use 1 for Tk-like export

# rows
::tkutils::tkutablelist::insert    $w row ?id?
::tkutils::tkutablelist::setRows   $w rows ?-ids idList?
::tkutils::tkutablelist::rows      $w
::tkutils::tkutablelist::getRow    $w index
::tkutils::tkutablelist::setRow    $w index row
::tkutils::tkutablelist::deleteRow $w index
::tkutils::tkutablelist::clear     $w
::tkutils::tkutablelist::size      $w

# cells
::tkutils::tkutablelist::cellText  $w row col
::tkutils::tkutablelist::setCell   $w row col value

# columns
::tkutils::tkutablelist::setColumns      $w {titles}
::tkutils::tkutablelist::columns         $w
::tkutils::tkutablelist::configureColumn $w col  -sortmode integer -align right ...
::tkutils::tkutablelist::configureRow    $w row  -foreground gray -background ...
::tkutils::tkutablelist::configureCell   $w r,c  -background yellow -foreground ...

# selection
::tkutils::tkutablelist::selection    $w        ;# selected row indices
::tkutils::tkutablelist::selectedRows $w        ;# selected rows
::tkutils::tkutablelist::selectRows   $w {i...}   ;# first row active and visible

# stable row ids (row -name)
::tkutils::tkutablelist::rowId       $w index     ;# -> id or ""
::tkutils::tkutablelist::findId      $w id        ;# -> index or -1
::tkutils::tkutablelist::selectedIds $w
::tkutils::tkutablelist::selectIds   $w {id...}   ;# -> ids found

# sorting / data sources
::tkutils::tkutablelist::sortBy   $w col ?-increasing|-decreasing?
::tkutils::tkutablelist::loadCsv  $w csv ?-header 0|1? ?-delimiter ,?
::tkutils::tkutablelist::fromNotes $w store ?-indent 0|1?   ;# a tunotes store
::tkutils::tkutablelist::tableWidget $w

# CSV export / edit hook
::tkutils::tkutablelist::toCsv   $w ?-header 0|1? ?-all 0|1? ?-formatted 0|1? ?tucsv options?
::tkutils::tkutablelist::saveCsv $w file ?toCsv options? ?-encoding utf-8?
::tkutils::tkutablelist::editEndCommand $w cmd             ;# cmd: path row col text -> new text
.CE
.SH "selection / activation callbacks"
.PP
::tkutils::tkutablelist::selectCommand $w ?cmd?           ;# get or set ::tkutils::tkutablelist::doubleCommand $w ?cmd?           ;# get or set
.CS

## Row ids, sorting, CSV

Row indices change when the user sorts. `insert … id` and `setRows … -ids`
store an id in the row's `-name`; `findId`, `selectedIds` and `selectIds` work
with ids; `selectedIds` leaves out selected rows without an id, use
`curselection` for all selected rows. `setRows` inserts all rows in one `insertlist` and re-applies the
current sort order. With `-ids`, the list needs one id per row.

With `-sortable 1` a header click calls `tablelist::sortByColumn` (toggles the
order, shows the arrow, sends `<<TablelistColumnSorted>>`); Shift+click adds
further sort columns (`tablelist::addToSortColumns`).

`toCsv` exports what the user sees: viewable rows and visible columns, raw
cell values. `-all 1` takes every row and column, `-formatted 1` the displayed
values. Other options go to `tclutils::tucsv::text`, e.g. `-delimiter ;` or
`-profile excel-de` (`;`, CRLF, BOM). `saveCsv` writes UTF-8 unless
`-encoding` says otherwise.

```tcl
::tkutils::tkutablelist::setRows $w $rows -ids $ids
::tkutils::tkutablelist::selectIds $w [list $currentId]
::tkutils::tkutablelist::saveCsv $w out.csv -profile excel-de
.CE
.SS "Row / cell formatting"
.PP
\fBconfigureRow\fR and \fBconfigureCell\fR are thin pass\-throughs to Tablelist's \fBrowconfigure\fR/\fBcellconfigure\fR (mirroring \fBconfigureColumn\fR). \fBrow\fR may be a row index, \fBend\fR, or a full key (see Hierarchy); \fBcell\fR is \fB"row,col"\fR. They accept the usual \fB\-foreground\fR/\fB\-background\fR/\fB\-font\fR options and return the target.
.SS "Footer (summary row)"
.PP
With \fB\-footer 1\fR, \fBwidget\fR adds a second single\-row tablelist directly below the table body and above the horizontal scrollbar. The wrapper keeps both in sync coherently: the table's \fB\-xscrollcommand\fR updates the scrollbar \fBand\fR mirrors the footer's horizontal position (it does not get overwritten), and the footer clones the table's column widths, alignment, \fB\-hide\fR flags and \fB\-titlecolumns\fR on creation and on every column resize/move. So footer totals stay aligned under their columns even while scrolling, and the scrollbar keeps working.
.CS
set w [::tkutils::tkutablelist::widget .t -columns {Article Qty Price} \
           -titlecolumns 1 -footer 1]

::tkutils::tkutablelist::footerWidget $w        ;# -> $w.foot  (or "" if no footer)
::tkutils::tkutablelist::footerSet    $w {Sum: 18 7,70}        ;# one value per column
::tkutils::tkutablelist::footerSum    $w -columns {1 2} -label Sum: -labelcolumn 0 ?-format %.2f?
.CE
.PP
\fBfooterSum\fR totals the given columns (German\-aware via \fBtclutils::tunum\fR, like \fBtkutlfooter::autosum\fR) and writes each sum under its own column, with \fB\-label\fR in \fB\-labelcolumn\fR. \fB\-format\fR applies Tcl \fB[format]\fR to the sum (English dot) \-\- for locale\-specific currency output, compute the strings yourself and use \fBfooterSet\fR.
.SS "Hierarchy (parent / child rows)"
.CS
set key [::tkutils::tkutablelist::insertChild $w parent values ?index?]
::tkutils::tkutablelist::expand   $w ?row?     ;# no row -> expand every row
::tkutils::tkutablelist::collapse $w ?row?     ;# no row -> collapse every row
.CE
.PP
\fBparent\fR is \fBroot\fR or a full key; \fBinsertChild\fR returns the \fBfull key\fR of the new row (\fBk0\fR, \fBk1\fR, …), which you pass as the next \fBparent\fR and to \fBconfigureRow\fR to colour the row. \fBexpand\fR/\fBcollapse\fR take a row index or key, or operate on all rows when called with no row.
.CS
set a [::tkutils::tkutablelist::insertChild $w root  {Level1 ...}]
set b [::tkutils::tkutablelist::insertChild $w $a    {Level2 ...}]
::tkutils::tkutablelist::configureRow $w $a -foreground darkblue
::tkutils::tkutablelist::expand $w
.CE
.SS Callbacks
.PP
\fB\-selectcommand\fR fires on \fB<<TablelistSelect>>\fR as \fBcmd $w $row\fR, where \fB$row\fR is the first selected row index, or \fB\-1\fR when the selection is empty. \fB\-doublecommand\fR fires on a double\-click on a data row as \fBcmd $w $row\fR, only when the click lands on a row (header/empty space is ignored). The click position is resolved with \fBtablelist::convEventFields\fR, so the row is correct regardless of stripes or separators. Both default to \fB""\fR (no callback). They can also be set or read at runtime with \fBselectCommand\fR/\fBdoubleCommand\fR.
.PP
The callback intentionally passes only the row index; fetch the row data via the existing API (\fBrows\fR, \fBgetRow\fR, \fBcellText\fR). When \fB\-editable 1\fR is also used, prefer \fB\-selectcommand\fR for row activation, since double\-click may overlap with in\-cell editing.
.PP
Declarative columns: a \fB\-columns\fR entry may be a plain title (spaces allowed) or a list \fB{title \-align right \-width N \-sortmode integer \-editable 1 ...}\fR:
.CS
set w [::tkutils::tkutablelist::widget .w \
    -columns {Name {Age -sortmode integer -align right} {Full Name}}]
.CE
.PP
Editing: with \fB\-editable 1\fR (or \fBconfigureColumn $w col \-editable 1\fR), double\-click a cell to edit it; \fBrows\fR/\fBgetRow\fR then reflect the new value.
.SS Errors
.PP
\fBsetRows\fR raises \fB{TKUTILS TKUTABLELIST OPTION <opt>}\fR for an unknown option and \fB{TKUTILS TKUTABLELIST IDS}\fR when the number of ids does not match.
.PP
Unknown widget options raise \fB{TKUTILS TKUTABLELIST OPTION <opt>}\fR with the message \fBunknown option "<opt>"\fR and a second line \fBKnown:\fR listing the valid options (since 2026\-10\-20; before without the option name).
.SS Launcher
.CS
tclsh bin/tkutablelist.tcl
.CE
